Cell[TextData[{
 "\tThe following considerations are helpful to interpolate the plots above \
and get a better picture of the system as a function of \[Mu]. For values of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Mu]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "94e42bb6-718e-4bf5-af9c-c73146bc2758"],
 " less than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "2"}], "\[Sigma]"}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", "2"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "12697e9f-6a11-47dc-8b92-677f7b930550"],
 ", an agent is unlikely to find one it likes more than being single, and the \
behavior of the system will be very similar to that of the last figure above. \
On the other extreme, if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ">", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Sigma]"}]}], "=", "2"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "e59b3731-0adc-45ff-96b7-378403da613f"],
 "$, agents will prefer to date any other agent than being single as they did \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Sigma]"}], "=", "2"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "8015dbc0-10c4-4616-b610-5eefeeb51fc0"],
 ", and the dynamics will be very similar to that of the first figure above. \
The difference, in this case, will be that the average utility will range on \
a different scale set by \[Mu]. Because for all values we have the average \
utility in the system with marriage higher than in the system without it, we \
are confident in concluding that this is a robust feature of our model. \
Therefore, the advice we extracted seems to hold in more general contexts."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.835780378515836*^9, 3.835780400900141*^9}, {
  3.838211692820509*^9, 3.838211822972039*^9}, {3.83821191519788*^9, 
  3.838211915913814*^9}, {3.8382120854770527`*^9, 
  3.83821208667487*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b7748c75-79a8-4b65-b08a-\
4ca35c24afc8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.3.3. Homogeneity", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.835780116391629*^9, 3.835780128238942*^9}, {
   3.8357802510558453`*^9, 3.835780253671085*^9}, {3.8382119914792843`*^9, 
   3.838212011318714*^9}, 
   3.838213000036319*^9},ExpressionUUID->"38eb6f38-f0d5-44d0-8358-\
f8ad2bf59248"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Another objection to the results presented in the previous section is that \
the assumption of a homogeneous society is clearly false. What is \
interesting, however, is that for a finite number of agents, this homogeneity \
is already broken. More precisely, for all agents ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "72913b5e-daf6-4043-911a-d38c1880498f"],
 ", its affinity with the other agents is given by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["A", "jk"], ":", 
        RowBox[{"1", "\[LessEqual]", "j", "\[LessEqual]", "n"}]}], " ", "&"}],
       " ", "j"}], "\[NotEqual]", "k"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "bc5f0380-ce44-49aa-a0a7-52e3f1f1bb55"],
 ", which is generated by the same distribution but is, in general, a \
different collection of numbers for each agent. To make this point more clear \
consider the following. We run a simulation"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.83821197962638*^9, {3.838212102522943*^9, 3.838212198073811*^9}, {
   3.8382123570871897`*^9, 3.83821240002923*^9}, {3.838212492123399*^9, 
   3.838212539669632*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1d08b994-8566-4ff8-b053-\
5fac1ddc508d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"r", "=", 
   RowBox[{"DatingMarriageModel", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\"\<N\>\"", ",", "10000", ",", "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", "\[Mu]s", 
     ",", "\[Sigma]s", ",", "\[CapitalLambda]", ",", "T"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.838212543803084*^9, 3.8382125450698147`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[199]:=",ExpressionUUID->"858f0f04-a58d-4c07-8b38-df5dca808de7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can select all agents ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "918c870b-47f7-4097-874e-38cee370770e"],
 " such that the average of the collection ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["A", "jk"], ":", 
        RowBox[{"1", "\[LessEqual]", "j", "\[LessEqual]", "n"}]}], " ", "&"}],
       " ", "j"}], "\[NotEqual]", "k"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"c965a559-32c4-410a-b60c-d608ab9c0d62"],
 " is larger than a certain positive value. We can pick this value in a way \
that we have just 5 percent of all agents selected"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.838212532839919*^9, 3.8382125349928513`*^9}, {
  3.838212570980364*^9, 3.838212571157331*^9}, {3.838215146149745*^9, 
  3.838215146214465*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"39de4cd9-6fdc-4c63-b1f8-\
620be65d2687"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Liked", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", 
    RowBox[{"SortBy", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"k", ",", 
          RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
            "r", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "1", "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], 
            "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "k", "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], "]"}]}], 
         "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"k", ",", "1", ",", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "r", "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", "1", "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}], 
           "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "Last"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
   "\[LeftDoubleBracket]", 
   RowBox[{"1", ";;", 
    RowBox[{"5", 
     FractionBox["n", "100"]}]}], "\[RightDoubleBracket]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.838212270165885*^9, 3.838212330243948*^9}, {
